---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Benchmark from '../../components/visuals/Benchmark.astro';
import RecallDemo from '../../components/visuals/RecallDemo.astro';
import { mailto } from '../../data/site';

const pipelines = [
  {
    name: 'Retrieval-only search',
    steps: ['Question', 'Embed it', 'Fetch the top k similar chunks', 'Model writes the answer'],
  },
  {
    name: 'Tool-calling agent',
    steps: ['Question', 'Model picks a tool', 'Tool queries the data', 'Model writes the answer'],
  },
];

const lessons = [
  {
    title: 'Match the tool to the question.',
    body: 'Search is great at “find the passage about X”. It is the wrong tool for “give me all of them”.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Count before you commit.',
    body: 'A design can look right in a demo and still miss most of the answer. You only find out by counting.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Keep the harness.',
    body: 'The test that settles an argument is also the one that catches the next regression.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="We almost shipped search · Yohann Pittappillil"
  description="Case study: how a head-to-head evaluation of a tool-calling agent against retrieval-only search settled the core architecture of an enterprise AI platform."
>
  <article class="cs">
    <header class="cs-hero container scrim">
      <a class="back link-arrow" href="/#work"><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">←</span><span>Selected work</span></a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · Mark Anthony Group · 2026</p>
      <h1 class="cs-title">We almost shipped search. <span class="muted">Then I counted.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        How a head-to-head evaluation settled the core architecture of an enterprise AI platform, and why “list every X”
        questions break retrieval.
      </p>
      <dl class="meta">
        <div><dt>My part</dt><dd>Designed and wrote the evaluation harness</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Platform</dt><dd>Enterprise agentic AI on Snowflake</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Compared</dt><dd>Tool-calling agent vs retrieval-only search</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <section class="cs-section container" aria-labelledby="cs-designs">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2 id="cs-designs" class="cs-h2">Two reasonable designs</h2>
        <p>
          The platform has to answer questions that cross data which used to live in separate places. There were two
          sensible ways to build it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Retrieval-only search</strong> turns documents and records into embeddings, finds the chunks most similar
          to the question, and hands them to the model. It is simple, cheap, and the default in most tutorials.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>A tool-calling agent</strong> gives the model tools that query the data directly and lets it decide
          which ones to call. More moving parts, more to test.
        </p>
        <p>Both are defensible. Rather than debate it, I measured it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="pipes" data-reveal>
        {
          pipelines.map((p, pi) => (
            <figure class:list={['pipe card', { em: pi === 1 }]}>
              <figcaption class="mono">{p.name}</figcaption>
              <ol role="list">
                {p.steps.map((s, i) => (
                  <li style={`--i:${i}`}>
                    <span>{s}</span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </figure>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section container" aria-labelledby="cs-question">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2 id="cs-question" class="cs-h2">The question that decides it</h2>
        <p>
          Plenty of questions are needles: “what’s the returns policy?” One good passage answers it, and search is
          excellent at finding one good passage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Businesses also ask for lists: “which ones”, “every”, “all of them”. The answer isn’t one passage. It’s every
          record that matches, and search has no idea how many that is. Try it:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="wide" data-reveal>
        <RecallDemo />
      </div>

      <div class="cs-text">
        <p>
          Search ranks by similarity and stops at <em>k</em>. However good the ranking, it can’t return more than
          <em>k</em> items, and “similar to the question” isn’t the same as “matches the question”. An agent with a query
          tool doesn’t guess. It asks the data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section container" aria-labelledby="cs-test">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2 id="cs-test" class="cs-h2">How I tested it</h2>
        <p>
          I wrote an evaluation harness that ran the same questions through both designs and scored every answer on one
          thing: did it include everything it should have?
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="chart card" data-reveal>
        <Benchmark uid="cs" autoplay caption={false} />
      </div>

      <div class="cs-text">
        <p>
          On list-style questions, the agent found everything. Search found about a fifth. That settled the platform’s
          core architecture.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cs-section container" aria-labelledby="cs-lessons">
      <div class="cs-text">
        <h2 id="cs-lessons" class="cs-h2">What I took from it</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="lessons" role="list">
        {
          lessons.map((l, i) => (
            <li class="card" data-reveal style={`--d:${i}`}>
              <p class="mono">0{i + 1}</p>
              <h3>{l.title}</h3>
              <p>{l.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>

    <aside class="cs-cta container" aria-label="Get in touch">
      <p class="cta-q">Have an AI decision that deserves a benchmark instead of a debate?</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={mailto('An AI decision worth benchmarking')}>Say hi</a>
        <a class="link-arrow" href="/#work"><span>More of my work</span><span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .cs {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + clamp(2.5rem, 1.5rem + 4vw, 5rem));
  }

  .cs-hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    justify-items: start;
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 2rem + 4vw, 6rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }

  .back {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
  }

  .back:hover .arr {
    transform: translateX(-4px);
  }

  .cs-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.4rem + 4.4vw, 5rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.042em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  :global(html.motion) .cs-hero > * {
    animation: cs-rise 0.9s var(--ease-out) both;
  }

  :global(html.motion) .cs-hero > :nth-child(2) {
    animation-delay: 60ms;
  }

  :global(html.motion) .cs-hero > :nth-child(3) {
    animation-delay: 120ms;
  }

  :global(html.motion) .cs-hero > :nth-child(4) {
    animation-delay: 180ms;
  }

  :global(html.motion) .cs-hero > :nth-child(5) {
    animation-delay: 240ms;
  }

  @keyframes cs-rise {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(16px);
    }
  }

  .meta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .meta dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--faint);
  }

  .meta dd {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .cs-section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 2.5rem + 4vw, 6rem);
  }

  .cs-text {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.125rem;
    max-width: var(--w-prose);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1rem + 0.3vw, 1.1875rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .cs-text strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 620;
  }

  .cs-h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.3rem + 1.8vw, 2.75rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.032em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .wide {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .pipes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .pipes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .pipe {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
  }

  .pipe figcaption {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .pipe.em figcaption {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .pipe ol {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pipe li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0 0 1.25rem 1.75rem;
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  .pipe li:last-child {
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .pipe li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.3em;
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--hair-strong);
    background: var(--bg-elev);
  }

  .pipe.em li::before {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--accent);
  }

  .pipe li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 5px;
    top: calc(0.3em + 13px);
    bottom: 2px;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--hair-strong);
  }

  .chart {
    max-width: 52rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 1rem + 2vw, 2.5rem);
    border-radius: var(--r-xl);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }

  .lessons {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    .lessons {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .lessons li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    align-content: start;
    padding: 1.75rem;
  }

  .lessons .mono {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .lessons h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .lessons p:last-child {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--fs-small);
  }

  .cs-cta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 3rem + 5vw, 8rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }

  .cta-q {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 1.2rem + 2.2vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: -0.032em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
